{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the amplitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6002dfd3c472c2f47574250b1a8d713956a737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 4 \\sin (x) + 3 \\cos (x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7bbd878610a4864fc8b42211b95adf44f65381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a \\cos \\theta + b \\sin \\theta)^2 \\le (a^2 + b^2)(\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta) = a^2 + b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"434\" height=\"22\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7f96a22647df72acccc70eb0884413ac7f9025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\cos \\theta +b \\sin \\theta \\le \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"212\" height=\"21\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1660d43b4960efd50409826b189fce815544ca22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=0$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />, then the expression is equal to zero for any angle. Otherwise, we can construct a right triangle with an angle measuring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729acb7391552a1f8d893217944a9d7004a5b32b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Evaluating the trig functions for this angle yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331fb0b57217af64d2fbfa5aee2203f223a32a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c851875c991472c46fdaaca1c02b2e2d0aceb011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta=\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a^2}{b^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"112\" height=\"44\" />, and multiplying the cosine by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and the since by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and adding yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47a020d22db4148650a1cfc4508d43e2d5238657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos \\theta +b \\sin \\theta=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"212\" height=\"21\" />. Plugging in 3 and 4, we find that the maximum value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since this is a trig function with midline <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, its amplitude is equal to its maximum value, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897a203bdf45af36f2b9edc59c3bc0beeb898be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/